// C11 6.7p3: a block-scope object without linkage is declared once per
// block (a `static` local too). The duplicate reached c2mir, whose check
// ("repeated declaration x") was the only thing refusing it — so the
// front end's own diagnostics (madcide's Problems panel) never saw it.
// Now refused where the declarator binds (Program::declare_object).
// Oracle: gcc and clang "redefinition of 's'" (g++ "redeclaration").
#include <stdio.h>
int main(void)
{
	static int s = 1;
	static int s = 2;
	printf("%d\n", s);
	return 0;
}
